hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16174","Hujayn ibn al-Muthanna Abu Umar narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Aziz, meaning Ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Salamah, narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn al-Fadl, from Sulayman ibn Yasar, from Jafar ibn Amr al-Damri, he said: I went out with Ubaydillah ibn Adi ibn al-Khiyar to Sham. When we came to Hims, Ubaydillah said to me: Hast thou interest in Wahshi, we ask him about the killing of Hamzah? I said: Yes, and Wahshi dwelt in Hims. He said: So we asked about him, and it was said to us: He is there in the shade of his palace, as though a wineskin. He said: So we came until we stood over him, and greeted, and he returned the greeting. He said: And Ubaydillah was veiled with his turban; Wahshi saw only his eyes and feet. So Ubaydillah said: O Wahshi, dost thou know me? He said: So he looked at him then said: No, by Allah, except that I know that Adi ibn al-Khiyar married a woman called Umm Qital daughter of Abi al-Is, and she bore him a boy in Makkah, and he sought a wet-nurse for him, so I carried that boy with his mother and handed him to her, so as though I looked at thy feet. He said: So Ubaydillah uncovered his face, then said: Wilt thou not inform us of the killing of Hamzah? He said: Yes, Hamzah killed Tuaymah ibn Adi at Badr, so my master Jubayr ibn Mutim said to me: If thou kill Hamzah for my uncle, thou art free. When the people went out on the day of Uhaynayn, he said: And Uhaynayn is a hill under Uhud with a valley between, I went out with the people to battle. When they arrayed for battle, he said: Siba came out: Who will duel? He said: So Hamzah ibn Abd al-Muttalib went out to him. So Siba ibn Umm Anmar said: O son of the cutter of clitorises, dost thou oppose Allah and His Messenger? Then he charged him and was as yesterday gone. And I lay in wait for Hamzah under a rock, until when he passed me, when he drew near me I threw him with my spear and put it in his groin until it came out between his thighs. He said: So that was the last covenant with him. He said: When the people returned I returned with them. He said: So I stayed in Makkah until Islam spread in it. He said: Then I went out to Taif. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to me. He said: And it was said to him: He does not harm envoys. He said: So I went out with them until I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: When he saw me he said: Art thou Wahshi? He said: I said: Yes. He said: Thou killed Hamzah? He said: I said: What was of the matter has reached thee, O Messenger of Allah. When he said: Canst thou hide thy face from me? He said: So I returned. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) died and Musaylimah the liar went out, he said: I said: I will go out to Musaylimah, perhaps I kill him and requite with him Hamzah. He said: So I went out with the people, and there was of their matter what was. He said: And there was a man standing in a breach of a wall, as though a dusky camel, with disheveled head. He said: So I threw him with my spear and put it between his breasts until it came out between his shoulders. He said: And a man of the Ansar leapt to him. He said: So he struck him with the sword on his head."
"16175","Abdullah ibn al-Fadl said: So Sulayman ibn Yasar informed me that he heard Abdullah ibn Umar, and a slave girl said on a roof, and the Commander of the Believers, the black slave killed him."
"16176","Yazid ibn Abd Rabbihi narrated to us, he said: al-Walid ibn Muslim narrated to us, from Wahshi ibn Harb, from his father, from his grandfather, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): We eat and are not full. He said: Perhaps you eat separated. Gather over your food and mention the name of Allah Almighty over it; it will be blessed for you in it."
